.TH RMUT-EGUI 1 "October 2026" "rmut 2.16.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rmut\-egui \- rmut, the mutt-like mail client, in a window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmut\-egui
.RB [ \-R ]
.RB [ \-e
.IR CMD ]...
.RB [ \-p | \-y ]
.RB [ \-z | \-Z ]
.RB [[ \-f ]
.IR MAILDIR " | " MBOX " | " imap:ACCOUNT [/ FOLDER ]]
.br
.B rmut\-egui
.B \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rmut\-egui
is the window front end over the same session as
.BR rmut (1):
the same mailboxes, the same keys, the same configuration file and
muttrc import, drawn with egui instead of a terminal. Everything
.BR rmut (1)
says about mailboxes, keys, patterns, hooks, sending and the
.BR [mail] ", " [pager] " and " [colors]
sections holds here; this page covers what the window adds or does
differently.
.PP
With no mailbox named it opens the one
.BR rmut (1)
would. The window appears at once and the mailbox opens behind a
progress line; keys typed meanwhile wait for it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-read\-only
Open the mailbox read-only.
.TP
.B \-y
Start in the folder browser.
.TP
.B \-p
Start by recalling a postponed message.
.TP
.BI \-e " CMD"
Run a configuration command after the configuration is read, as
.BR rmut (1)
does; may be given more than once.
.TP
.BI \-f " MAILBOX"
The mailbox to open, as the plain argument names it.
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-Z
Exit with status 1, before any window opens, when the mailbox holds
no messages
.RB ( \-z )
or no new ones
.RB ( \-Z ).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.PP
Send mode
.RB ( \-s ", " \-a ", " \-c ", " \-b ", " \-i ", " \-\- )
needs a terminal and is refused here; use
.BR rmut (1).
So is a
.I mailto:
URL: the window takes a mailbox, not a draft.
.SH THE WINDOW
The four regions of
.BR rmut (1)
are all here: the help bar, the index or the message, the status
bar, and the message line with prompts, notes and errors. Around the
keys, the window adds:
.TP
.B The mouse
A click selects a message, a double click opens it; in a message,
the mini-index above it switches messages the same way. A URL in a
message opens with a click
.RB ( "[ui] url_command" ).
The scroll wheel scrolls, and the pager's scrollbar drags.
.TP
.B Menus
A menu bar (Mailbox, Message, Tagged, Thread, Sort, Help) offers
the common functions by name, with their keys, and a right click on a
message offers what applies to it.
.TP
.B Zoom
Ctrl+= and Ctrl+\- zoom the whole window, Ctrl+0 resets it, and so do
Ctrl with the wheel and a trackpad pinch. The zoom is remembered.
.TP
.B Preferences
Mailbox \(-> Preferences sets the text size, the font, the canvas
colors, the editor, the proportional body, inline images and HTML
rendering, applied at once. Saving writes them to
.IR gui.toml ,
never to the hand-written configuration.
.TP
.B Viewers
A part opened with a mailcap viewer is written to a private
directory of its own; a viewer that needs a terminal runs in the
.B [gui] terminal
emulator, and any other runs as a window of its own while the mail
window carries on. The copy goes when the viewer exits, or when the
window closes.
.TP
.B Leaving
However the window closes (q, its close button, Alt+F4, the window
manager, SIGTERM, or Ctrl+C in the terminal it was started from), it
leaves the way q does: mail still waiting out
.B undo_send
goes, and so do the flag changes a quit writes.
.SH EDITING
.B [gui] editor
chooses where a draft is written:
.TP
.B external
(the default) runs
.B $EDITOR
in the
.B [gui] terminal
emulator, as
.BR rmut (1)
runs it in its own terminal.
.TP
.B builtin
edits in a text box inside the window; Ctrl+Enter finishes, Esc
abandons.
.TP
.B nvim
embeds Neovim
.RB ( "nvim \-\-embed" ,
which must be on
.BR PATH )
in the window: a full Neovim with your configuration, drawn in the
message area. Leaving it with :wq goes on to the compose menu;
:cq, like any editor failing, keeps the draft and says so.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The
.B [gui]
section of
.I ~/.config/rmut/config.toml
belongs to the window; the terminal never reads it. Every key is
optional.
.TP
.B size
Text size in points (14).
.TP
.B font
A .ttf or .otf file for the monospace face (egui's own when unset).
.TP
.B terminal
The emulator that hosts
.BR $EDITOR ,
.B !
commands and terminal viewers
.RB ( $TERMINAL ,
then foot, alacritty, kitty, xterm).
.TP
.BR background ", " foreground
The canvas and its default ink, as color names or
.BR #rrggbb .
Bold is drawn by moving the ink away from the canvas, so it reads on
light canvases and dark ones alike.
.TP
.B editor
.BR external " (default), " builtin " or " nvim ;
see EDITING.
.TP
.B proportional
The message body in a proportional face; the index, the headers and
indented (preformatted) lines stay monospace. Off by default.
.TP
.B inline_images
image/* parts drawn in the message, under their
.B [\-\- Type: image/... \-\-]
markers. On by default.
.TP
.B html
The window's own say over
.BR "[pager] html" ,
so the terminal can keep one way and the window another.
.TP
.B [gui.colors]
Window-only overrides of
.BR [colors] :
the same keys and values, plus
.BR #rrggbb .
.PP
.I gui.toml
beside the configuration file holds what the Preferences dialog
saved; it is read over the
.B [gui]
section, so the dialog wins over the hand-written values it covers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rmut/config.toml
The configuration, shared with
.BR rmut (1)
.RB ( $RMUT_CONFIG
overrides).
.TP
.I ~/.config/rmut/gui.toml
The Preferences dialog's saved values.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/rmut/gui-zoom
The remembered zoom
.RB ( $XDG_CACHE_HOME
overrides the parent).
.TP
.I rmut-egui.desktop
The menu entry, in the release archive and in the source's
.IR crates/rmut-egui/dist ;
.B just install-desktop
installs it with
.B Exec
pinned to the installed binary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the window closes normally; 1 when the mailbox could not be
opened, and for
.BR \-z " and " \-Z
as above.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmut (1),
.BR mutt (1),
.BR nvim (1)
